ngs on Monday night. Then it turns into a nostalgia week: Blizzard relaunches 2004 and Nintendo remakes 1998. Mon Nov 2: Apple reports fiscal Q4 after the close – analysts expect $1.98 a share vs $1.85 a year ago. Listen for iPhone demand and what Tim Cook says about Siri and AI. Mon Nov 2: Palantir reports the same evening – it guided to about $2.16B in revenue. The stock is priced for perfection, so a small miss will hurt. Tue Nov 3: AMD reports after the bell – guidance was around $13B, up from $11.5B last quarter. The data center GPU number is the whole story. Wed Nov 4: World of Warcraft: Forever goes live – a permanent classic-style WoW with a new race, 1,000+ new quests and nine dungeons. Included with a regular sub. Wed Nov 4: Qualcomm and Arm report after the close – two quick reads on the phone market and on who gets paid for every chip in it. Thu Nov 5: The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time remake lands on Switch 2 – fully voiced, $59.99 digital, $69.99 physical. Probably the best reason yet to own the console. Thu Nov 5: Motorola Signature 27 launches globally – 200MP periscope with up to 100x zoom and seven years of Android updates. Motorola wants a seat at the flagship table. See it coming.","image":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/ZJUKCWu5oBsqmMI6xDWe3c6wT3XtAHcDy4c_kdYuZXhlBwTbEAmzwpmxKnwERUjYfvMmphMp2wIzOoCmncj65hLNb68HyK_Jc4BKq6RxGrcmpSBko6bIm1rtZorFA1VQCgeUWf_GcfTFH_xMvPjPw4t5FVaevj4wFFz-RlXAVFeZn_XdnE_wgx-Uk5WppxtdfK_KsiPQ1rBJDAGzwkGM4NwXkiuqPDSTuA_8WMrZ-qyyEFbOkphme66ofTMuzSvKCp-4kKwFiJSEYqWTEufpE4ZRF_NrRu11d8RMTSLZei52mp6jHjbu_LUjpz4bCXPSf71v3sSSVquuH1HnqYBcYQ.jpg","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"680","date":"2026-11-01T18:04:24+00:00","text":"All the leaks for the Portal prequel F-Stop have been compiled into a playable game Read on Engadget","image":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/PCpLE9wQ_Up-T6egmYKg9qhmlGw3aHWN1e0ChtjpaHpPptNT4sDNVgFym81SKsxJsm3Wkko2frLT6DDr5O6g-VhAMYJqV9kLS5BZEgt8sX7JalTzcs9mn6rWgIPKAfZLqQ93YIKwohFiOkgDvluJoKVBUrlw-Kkenpi6EM